				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/pbs.twimg.com/b4f9e999d049afc35ecceb237a2ddd0330049be667118285989a1b9f5f7b0991.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2019-07-12T16:33:38.000Z",
			"content": "Nice to know none of us struggle alone. Thanks for sharing. I have a fantastic job in a fantastic industry, but my brain increasingly feels like a lot of melted cheese 🧀",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
			"id": 660918,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://oliodigest.com/replies/Burnout-is-real/",
			"author": {
				"name": "Drei aka Bitcoin Master",
				"url": "https://oliodigest.com/",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/oliodigest.com/2acc8b4295a7864727af70049bc2440bb1dfa283c640d08f7e11f20a12220d6f.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2019-08-04T00:00:00.000Z",
			"content": "<p><a href=\"https://www.zachleat.com/web/burnout/\">Zach</a> is right. With all the things we can do online, especially if your profession is Internet-related, burnout is\na real thing and happens often. My last burnout happened when I finally achieved the savings I need to finance an IVF procedure for my wife. I was literally\nallergic to everything Internet - no Facebook, no emails, nothing, toally unplugged. The slower pace reset my state of mind.</p>",
			"type": "mention",
			"via": "webmention"
		}
	],
